  "extends": "_shared",
  "_comment": "A single trade, and the second one that opts out of part of the shared deny list. 'store' is in that list because everywhere else it means a counter with stock on it, but flooring is the trade where Google uses it for firms that install: a large share of real installers are filed as a flooring, carpet or tile STORE. deny_remove escapes exactly that word; shop, showroom, supply, supplies, supplier, wholesale, retail and materials stay denied, so a retailer is still refused. Hardwood installers are filed under 'wood floor installation service', so the shared installation-service rule is widened to let the flooring forms of it through. Carpet CLEANING stays in recurring_deny: it is a recurring service, not this trade.",
